    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0071" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00/1531</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dooman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1767</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-08">July 8, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to the Embassy’s telegram
                    no. 234, May 18, 5 p.m., in which there is given the text of a message from the
                    Prime <pb facs="0072" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/> Minister which was handed to
                    Ambassador Grew by the Minister for Foreign Affairs with the request that Mr.
                    Grew deliver the message personally to me. There is enclosed a reply to this
                    message.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d4-a1.xml" xpointer="d4-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
